    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOH2Qg5s8AAAABOcNW0g",
      "title": "miner: stop payload builder on miner shutdown",
      "author": "nonsense",
      "number": 817,
      "body": "The background payload builder in `miner/payload_building.go` logs `Stopping work on payload ... reason=miner-shutdown` when the miner's lifetime context is done, but it does not return. After `Miner.Close` cancels that context, the case is always ready, so the goroutine spins and logs the line until the end-of-build timer or a resolve stops it.\n\nThis hits the library use of op-geth. The optimism monorepo's op-e2e runs geth in-process and closes it at the end of each test. Every open payload then logs the line for 2 to 6 seconds, 50,000 to 190,000 times. A run of the fault-proof test job logs it 40,000 to 365,000 times, and its step log reaches CircleCI's 50 MB limit within minutes.\n\nThe builder now returns on miner shutdown, like on its other stop reasons. `TestBuildPayloadStopsOnMinerClose` counts the shutdown records of one payload after `Miner.Close`. It fails without the fix and passes with it.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
      "createdAt": "2026-11-11T17:39:59Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 46,
      "deletions": 0
    }
